Google Workspace OAuth auditing maps add-on permission URIs ( drive , gmail.* , admin.* ) to Google's official restricted , sensitive , and non-sensitive verification tiers so security teams can catch over-scoped Shadow SaaS automatically. Auditing the Top 100 popular-apps on Google Workspace Marketplace shows 42% request at least one Google Restricted OAuth scope and 21% combine high OAuth risk with >365 days since their last listing update . Below, you'll get the real 100-app security findings plus two zero-proxy automation patterns: querying Marketplace OAuth risks inside Claude / Cursor via Apify MCP , and running a weekly 5-node n8n Slack alert workflow . Transparency note: I built the Apify Actor used in this walkthrough ( Google Workspace Marketplace Scraper ). All stats come from running it live on popular-apps . Table of Contents Top 100 Marketplace OAuth Study Results Step 1: Audit Apps in Claude or Cursor via Apify MCP Step 2: Weekly OAuth and Review Alerts in n8n Why No Playwright Is Needed Try It and Share Feedback Top 100 Marketplace OAuth Study Results Instead of manually clicking through OAuth consent screens, we extracted the Top 100 apps in popular-apps via Jvccvctus/google-workspace-marketplace-scraper (finished in 32.4 seconds , $0.50 total at $5/1,000 apps all-inclusive, zero residential proxies). Metric (Top 100 Popular Apps, Nov 2026) Result Apps requesting ≥ 1 Google Restricted OAuth scope ( high risk) 42% Apps requesting Sensitive scopes only ( medium risk) 51% Apps requesting Non-Sensitive scopes only ( low risk) 7% Average / Median OAuth scopes per app 8.47 / 6.5 Apps with auth/script.external_request (external server calls) 43% Apps with auth/drive (full Drive read/write, Restricted ) 18% Apps with auth/admin.directory.user.readonly ( Restricted ) 18% Apps with High OAuth risk + > 365 days without listing update 21% Apps with Google's Verified Developer badge 55% Apps with ≥ 1 negative (1–2★) recent review 59% Top 10 Most Frequently Requested Scopes Rank OAuth Scope Google Tier Share of Top 100 1 auth/userinfo.email non-sensitive 100% 2 auth/userinfo.profile non-sensitive 100% 3 auth/script.external_request sensitive 43% 4 auth/script.container.ui non-sensitive 36% 5 auth/drive.file sensitive 26% 6 auth/script.scriptapp sensitive 25% 7 auth/spreadsheets sensitive 23% 8 auth/script.send_mail sensitive 19% 9 auth/drive restricted 18% 10 auth/admin.directory.user.readonly restricted 18% Why context matters: Enterprise governance platforms such as GAT+ (47 scopes, 26 restricted) or BetterCloud (38 scopes, 23 restricted) legitimately need Admin SDK access. The real audit priority is catching everyday Docs, PDF, or Sheets utilities asking for blanket auth/drive instead of per-file auth/drive.file — especially the 21% untouched for over a year. Step 1: Audit Apps in Claude or Cursor via Apify MCP The scraper runs with Limited permissions , making it discoverable and callable over Apify's hosted MCP server ( https://mcp.apify.com ). Every record returns oauthSummary , oauthScopes , reviewSummary , and a concise markdownSummary optimized for LLM context windows. MCP Client Configuration { "mcpServers" : { "apify-gwm" : { "type" : "http" , "url" : "https://mcp.apify.com/?tools=fetch-actor-details,Jvccvctus/google-workspace-marketplace-scraper" , "headers" : { "Authorization" : "Bearer YOUR_APIFY_API_TOKEN" } } } } Copy-Paste Security Audit Prompts Allowlist Screening (before approving an employee request): Inspect https://workspace.google.com/marketplace/app/bettercloud/800521135851 using Jvccvctus/google-workspace-marketplace-scraper and list every Google Restricted OAuth scope, whether the developer is verified, update freshness in days, and any recurring issues in recent 1-2 star reviews. Category Comparison: Find the top 10 Freemium Gmail & Google Sheets mail merge apps with at least 100,000 installs, rank them by OAuth riskLevel, and flag stale listings (>365 days). Sample Output Schema ( oauthSummary ) { "oauthSummary" : { "totalScopeCount" : 8 , "restrictedScopeCount" : 1 , "sensitiveScopeCount" : 3 , "nonSensitiveScopeCount" : 4 , "riskLevel" : "high" , "scopeUrls" : [ "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets" , "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send" ] } } Personal reviewer names and internal Gaia IDs are excluded intentionally so outputs stay GDPR-friendly . Step 2: Weekly OAuth and Review Alerts in n8n To run this audit automatically every Monday and forward only flagged apps ( high OAuth risk or recent 1–2★ reviews) to Slack, use the official @apify/n8n-nodes-apify community node ( Run actor and get dataset ). Workflow Architecture Schedule Trigger — Every Monday at 09:00. Apify ( Run actor and get dataset ) — Executes Jvccvctus~google-workspace-marketplace-scraper with maxTotalChargeUsd: 0.25 . IF Node — Checks oauthSummary.riskLevel === "high" OR reviewSummary.negativeReviewCount > 0 . Code Node — Builds a compact Slack alert digest with exact install counts ( installCountNumeric ) and Marketplace links. HTTP Request Node — Posts the digest to your Slack / Teams / Discord Webhook. Ready-to-Import n8n Workflow JSON (Includes Canvas Sticky Notes) { "name" : "Google Workspace Marketplace — Weekly OAuth Risk & Competitor Monitor" , "nodes" : [ { "parameters" : { "width" : 580 , "height" : 200 , "color" : 6 , "content" : "## 🛡️ Google Workspace OAuth & Competitor Audit
